# QA orchestration policy

You coordinate the QA subagents. Do the analysis yourself; delegate the rest.

During **analyze**, run live UI recon per jira-ticket-to-gherkin step 2 when creds are set. If creds are missing, produce Gherkin anyway and call out skipped recon.

## Skills

- **jira-ticket-to-gherkin** — a DS ticket into `features/<key>.feature`. Use this when a ticket exists.
- **explore-and-generate** — no ticket. One highest-value uncovered flow into `features/explore-<area>-<flow>.feature`. Do not use it when a ticket already exists.
- **self-heal** — locator drift only, after triage classifies a red run as a test issue. Never for a real app bug. See `.cursor/skills/self-heal/SKILL.md`.

## Routing

- ticket given → analyze (Jira + UI recon) → produce a test plan (`features/<key>.feature`)
- no ticket / "find what we're not testing" / "explore <page> for untested flows" / "expand coverage" → **explore-and-generate** → one feature file, then the plan-ready path
- plan ready → delegate to test-writer (programs page must include a11y per a11y-checks)
- spec returned → run: `npx playwright test` (respect `playwright.config.ts`: local `retries: 0`, CI `retries: 2`; do not add `workers: 1` or raise retries above 2 to green a run)
- run is red → delegate to triage → **Heal on red**
- never use `.disableRules()` to go green on a11y failures
- external backlog trigger → Backlog mode, one ticket at a time

## Heal on red

On a red run, delegate to **triage** to classify. Then:

- **Drift (test issue)** → apply **self-heal**: re-discover via the Agent-Browser, patch the POM, re-run to prove green with assertions unchanged, then open a repair PR linked to the run. Never heal an assertion. Never merge a repair without a human.
- **Real app bug** (including axe WCAG violations) → delegate to **bug-reporter** to file and link it — **never heal a bug**. Stop.
- Other test issues (not locator drift) → delegate to test-writer (propose a fix; human OKs).

**Budget.** At most 5 heals per run. If a heal will not prove green with assertions unchanged, stop and escalate — do not weaken asserts, delete expects, or keep patching.
## Backlog mode

The agent never decides when to start. A Cursor Automation, a headless `agent -p` run, or a local batch starts the run. Do not drain this queue on your own.

**Queue.** DS tickets in status "In Progress" that lack the `tests-generated` label:

```
project = DS AND status = "In Progress" AND (labels is EMPTY OR labels != "tests-generated") ORDER BY key ASC
```

**Budget.** At most 5 tickets per run. Leave the rest for the next trigger.

**Per ticket.** analyze → test-writer → `npx playwright test` → triage on red. The coordinator opens one PR for that ticket (test-writer still only writes under `tests/`, `pages/`, `fixtures/`). Put the DS key in the PR title and body. When the PR is open, add the `tests-generated` label on the ticket so the next run skips it.

**Repeated identical failure.** Never re-run that same failing spec again. Stop the ticket, leave its PR unmerged, add `tests-generated` if the PR is open, and move to the next ticket.

**Human gate.** Never merge a PR. Never close or transition the ticket. A human approves every merge and every filed bug.

## Loop guard

At most 3 delegations per task; never re-run an identical failing spec more than twice — then stop and ask. In backlog mode, stop that ticket and move on.

## Approval

A human approves any merge and any filed bug.

## Guardrails

- A human approves every merge and every filed bug — no subagent merges, and bug-reporter files only after a human confirms the defect.
- No subagent edits application source.
- Blast radius:
  - **test-writer** — writes test code only under `tests/`, `pages/`, `fixtures/`; no commits or PRs unless asked.
  - **triage** — read-only (`readonly: true`); reads CI logs, artifacts, and repo; returns a diagnosis, changes nothing.
  - **bug-reporter** — read-only on the repo (`readonly: true`); its only write is one Jira bug linked to the story.
  - **self-heal** — POM locator patches only under `pages/`; never edits assertions in `tests/`; opens a repair PR, never merges.

## Done

Single ticket: the suite is green, or a bug is filed and linked (including axe violations reported and stopped — never silenced with `.disableRules()`), or a locator-drift heal has an open unmerged repair PR linked to the run. Backlog run: each taken ticket has one open PR linked to the DS key and the `tests-generated` label, and nothing was merged or closed.

## Reliability report

After any coordinator/orchestrator run (local or CI-backed), regenerate **[`eval-report.md`](../eval-report.md)**:

```bash
npm run eval:report
# or with session context:
node scripts/eval-report.mjs --trigger local-orchestrator --session-note "DS-5 triage + heal"
```

Log **ask vs guess** and **heal** outcomes in `.eval-state/*.jsonl` when they occur (see `.eval-state/README.md`). CI runs the same script after **E2E Tests** and **Test generation** workflows and uploads the artifact `eval-report`.
